       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 400 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 200 mg/day. Higher doses carry a greater risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding effects. Nothing you've told me about the patient (70 kg, normal renal and hepatic function, no allergies) would justify going above that limit.\n\nWas this a typo? Here are some options:\n- **Usual dosing:** Start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, then titrate by 25\u201350 mg at intervals of at least a week. The usual range is 50\u2013200 mg daily.\n- **200 mg once daily:** I can enter this if the patient is already on a stable dose and you're targeting the maximum.\n- **400 mg:** If you intentionally want this dose, for example on the advice of psychiatry or a pharmacist, tell me. I can enter it with a note documenting the rationale and who approved it. I'd also suggest checking an ECG and the patient's other serotonergic and QT-prolonging medications first.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
